Here's a script that denies access to a website or service using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. This script creates a modal dialog that displays a denial message and includes a button to close the window.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Access Denied</title>
    <style>
        #denialModal {
            display: none;
            position: fixed;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            background-color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
            z-index: 1000;
        }
        #denialModal h2 {
            color: red;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        #denialModal p {
            color: #666;
            margin: 10px 0;
        }
        #closeButton {
            padding: 8px 16px;
            background-color: #ff4444;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
        #closeButton:hover {
            background-color: #cc0000;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="denialModal">
        <h2>Access Denied</h2>
        <p>This access has been denied. Please contact the website administrator for more information.</p>
        <button id="closeButton">Close</button>
    </div>

    <script>
        window.onload = function() {
            document.getElementById('denialModal').style.display = 'block';
        }

        document.getElementById('closeButton').addEventListener('click', function() {
            document.getElementById('denialModal').style.display = 'none';
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This script does the following:

1. Creates a modal dialog that appears immediately when the page loads.
2. Displays a denial message.
3. Includes a button to close the modal.
4. The modal has a professional appearance with a red theme and shadow effects.
5. The modal is centered on the screen and has a semi-transparent background overlay.

To use this script:

1. Copy the entire code into a new file with a `.html` extension.
2. Save it as `deny_access.html`
3. Open it in a web browser.

When you open the file, a modal will appear immediately with the denial message. The user will be unable to access the rest of the website or service until they close the modal.

Features:
- Responsive design
- Clean and professional look
- Easy to customize
- No server-side requirements
- Works in most modern browsers

You can customize the message, colors, and styling by modifying the CSS and HTML content to match your needs. The JavaScript handles the display and closing of the modal, making it simple to implement.

